    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Yes, standard homeowners insurance policies in Utah cover hail damage to your roof, siding, and the structure of your home, subject to your policy's deductible and terms.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Details for Utah Homeowners"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Covered Perils: Standard dwelling coverage pays for sudden and accidental damage caused by severe weather like hail, heavy wind, and fallen branches.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Deductibles: Many policies feature a separate, higher percentage deductible for wind and hail claims rather than a standard flat dollar amount. Check your specific policy declarations page.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Time Limits to File: Most Utah insurance policies give you one year from the date of the hailstorm to file a claim. However, waiting too long can make it harder to prove the damage came from that specific storm .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Age Exceptions: Insurers may restrict or reduce payouts if your roof is old (typically 15 to 20+ years) or if the damage is due to wear and tear rather than a specific storm event.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Discounts: Upgrading to Class 4 impact-resistant shingles can help lower your future insurance premiums in hail-prone areas."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          7,
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Recommended Next Steps"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Get an Independent Inspection: Contact a trusted local roofer or inspector before calling your insurance company to document whether the damage actually justifies a claim.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              9
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review Your Deductible: Check whether your wind/hail deductible is a flat fee or a percentage of your dwelling coverage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Check File Deadlines: Confirm your insurer's exact time frame (often 6 to 12 months) for reporting storm damage.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              10
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, I can help you:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Estimate how a percentage deductible affects a claim payout"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review what to look for during a roof inspection"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Understand how a hail claim might impact your insurance rates"
          }
        ]
      }
